  "name": "luh-2022-oakland-usec-in-sdps-replication",
  "notes": "Replication Package for the IEEE Symposium on Security and Privacy (Oakland '22) paper: \"How Does Usable Security (Not) End Up in Software Products? Results From a Qualitative Interview Study\"\r\n\r\nTo make our study reproducible and allow for easy access for meta-research, we publish a replication package containing the following documents: \r\n(1) The pre-questionnaire for demographic and quantitative questions; \r\n(2) The interview guide with the main questions and follow-up prompts for the semi-structured interviews; \r\n(3) The materials we used to contact and recruit participants; \r\n(4) The consent forms; \r\n(5) A table of the software used in this study; \r\n(6) The operationalized codebook with codes contributing to this paper.",
